Headless: give a label's live region

A frontend that draws labels itself needs a label's live region (setLabelLiveRegion(): off, polite or assertive) to
announce the label's changes as the desktop's screen reader support does. THeadlessSession::LabelContent did not carry
it. TLabelModel::setLiveRegion() already tells the view of a real change (AccessibilityChange::LiveRegion, from
Mudlet/Mudlet#12937), which TNullConsoleFrontend passes on, so a change names the label in scriptWindowsChanged.

This adds liveRegion to LabelContent, filled where accessibleName is, so a frontend reads it with the label's other
content. Tested in HeadlessSessionWindowsTest, and listed among labelContent()'s fields in docs/headless.md.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

